# chess-retro configuration — every line here is optional.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. With none of it set the app still works: it
# finds Stockfish on your PATH, keeps its database under data/, and runs every
# feature except the written coaching.
#
# Your chess.com username is NOT here — it lives in the database, set on the
# Settings page, so one install can hold more than one account's games.

# Where the SQLite database lives. Point it elsewhere to keep several corpora
# side by side.
# CHESS_RETRO_DB=data/chess-retro.db

# The Stockfish binary. Only needed when it is not on your PATH.
# STOCKFISH_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/stockfish

# Enables the written coaching on the dashboard. Without it the dashboard still
# ranks and explains your weaknesses from the statistics — the core feature is
# not gated behind a paid account. Read server-side only; never sent to the
# browser.
#
# A pay-as-you-go API key from console.anthropic.com/settings/keys — NOT a
# Claude.ai subscription, which will not work here. Calls Claude Sonnet 5 at
# under 2 cents per distinct ranking, cached so revisiting costs nothing.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Which model writes the coaching. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5, which matched
# Opus on every check that matters here at about a third of the cost. Set this
# to claude-opus-5 ($5/$25 per million) to use the model this was tuned on.
# CHESS_RETRO_COACH_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
